[rvn-ple] Refuse NEXTN on an RVN text checkpoint that ships no draft layer

rvn-w4a16 only. The gate fires when the config is an RVN text model
(architectures=Qwen4ExpForCausalLM and model_type=qwen4_exp_text), the
speculative algorithm is NEXTN (resolved to EAGLE) and no
--speculative-draft-model-path was given. The LIL multimodal
(Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration) path, STANDALONE and every external-draft
launch take the same return-None branch as before; no other architecture is
named.

Mechanism of the failure it prevents, read off the stacked tree:
  * configs/model_config.py:747-754 rewrites the draft architecture to
    Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP only when architectures[0] is
    Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration, so for the RVN text arch the rewrite
    never fires and the draft worker constructs the full 48-layer target
    model again (config.json: num_hidden_layers 48).
  * load_model_utils.py:281 is "if not is_draft_worker:", so that second copy
    never gets server_args.ple_offload_embedding copied onto hf_text_config.
    models/qwen4_exp.py:512-515 gates its meta-device defer on exactly that
    flag, so the defer is skipped and the n-gram table allocates on the device.

The size follows from the shipped config alone, not from the launch flags.
ngram_heads = (ngram_size - 1) * heads_per_ngram = (3 - 1) * 8 = 16
(qwen4_exp.py:458), and head_dim_per_ngram = ngram_embed_dim // ngram_heads =
2560 // 16 = 160 columns (:476, with embedding_dim = config.ple_embed_dim
carried through :969 into the constructor call at :973-976, which binds it as
the embedding_dim that becomes ngram_embed_dim at :455). The rows are the
per-head primes that _build_head_vocab_and_offsets walks with
sympy.nextprime from ngram_vocab_size_base - 1 = 19999999 (:559-571, :552-556),
padded up to make_ngram_vocab_size_divisible_by = 128 (:498-501): summed and
padded, that walk is 320001536 rows at ple_layer_index 0 - reproduced by
running the same sympy.nextprime chain. That index is the position of the layer
inside sorted(set(ple_layer_ids)), not the layer id, so this checkpoint's
ple_layer_ids [2] resolves to index 0 (:1356-1360) - feeding 2 in as the index
yields 320009088 and a different byte count.
ple_embedding_dtype is nvfp4, which selects params_dtype=float8_e4m3fn at 1
byte per element (:519-523): 320001536 x 160 = 47.6839 GiB at TP1.
Cross-check against the working target launch, which loads that same table as
26.8222 GiB of pinned host bytes - exactly 9/16 of 47.6839 GiB, the nvfp4
nibble-plus-e4m3-scale packing.

There is nothing for that draft to be, so the refusal is not conditioned on
the declared count. /models/rvn-qwen38-ple-nvfp4/config.json declares
architectures ["Qwen4ExpForCausalLM"], model_type "qwen4_exp_text",
mtp_num_hidden_layers 0 and no num_nextn_predict_layers, and its
model.safetensors.index.json weight_map holds 296,238 tensors of which zero
contain "mtp" anywhere. The contract agrees: Qwen4ExpForCausalLM calls
assert_rvn_text_config (models/qwen4_exp.py:3020) and then requires
rvn_mtp_count(config) == 0 (:3060), and its loader runs every weight name
through reject_non_text_weight_name, which raises on any name containing "mtp"
(models/qwen4_exp_text_adapter.py:174-183) for a config without the graft
stamp. A text checkpoint that did declare MTP layers would be stopped by the
bare :3060 assertion instead, so refusing here is better worded, not narrower.
rvn_mtp_count sums the two flat fields only; config.json also carries an mtp
sub-object whose num_hidden_layers is 0, and the contract deliberately does
not read it.

Gate reachability is verified rather than assumed: ModelConfig deep-copies
get_config(...) into hf_config (configs/model_config.py:310), the same object
server_args.get_model_config().hf_config hands the gate; the multimodal-name
rewrite at :325-330 keys on Qwen3_8FlashNextForConditionalGeneration alone, so
a text config cannot be aliased away before the gate reads it; and get_config
resolves model_type qwen4_exp_text to Qwen4ExpTextConfig
(configs/qwen4_exp.py:15-16). is_rvn_text_config reads only architectures and
model_type - the two fields assert_rvn_text_config already proved on this
checkpoint during the working target load - so the gate cannot be a no-op on a
launch that got as far as the draft worker.

Why the alternatives are wrong, not merely bigger:
  * Copying ple_offload_embedding onto the draft worker would pin a second
    26.8 GiB host table the draft cannot read: the intended draft sets
    config.ple_layer_ids = [] (models/qwen4_exp_mtp.py:46), PLE construction is
    gated on (layer_id + 1) in ple_layer_ids (models/qwen4_exp.py:1356) and
    has_ple = bool(config.ple_layer_ids) (:1804), so self.ple stays None and
    the table is never built. It would still leave a 48-layer duplicate of the
    target at the wrong depth.
  * Adding "Qwen4ExpForCausalLM" to that draft remap removes the allocation but
    leaves a draft with nothing to load: Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP defines no
    load_weights and inherits Qwen3_5ForCausalLMMTP.load_weights
    (models/qwen4_exp_mtp.py:28), while the checkpoint carries no model.mtp.*
    tensors. It would construct, "load" and serve an untrained head - a false
    pass against the acceptance line. That hunk would also have to keep the
    num_nextn_predict_layers = 1 rewrite inside the is_draft_model branch after
    the deepcopy at :752, since assert_rvn_text_config and :3060 read the
    target config too.

The two arch gaps this refuses around - the draft remap at
configs/model_config.py:747 and the list at arg_groups/speculative_hook.py
580-597 that defaults the draft path to the target path - are closed for the
graft-stamped candidate by patches 0058/0059, which widen the text contract
only when the config carries the rvn_mtp_graft stamp. This gate keeps refusing
the unstamped RVN text launch, which is the case where no draft exists. That
makes one ordering a cross-patch contract rather than an internal detail:
0059 defaults the draft path *above* rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported(), so a
stamped candidate reaches the gate with a non-None path and is allowed, while
an unstamped one still sees the refusal. That ordering is stated in 0059's own
comment; the gate cannot test it, since a stamped config is 0058's shape and
its own helper. What the regression file does pin is the internal half: the
refusal leaves speculative_draft_model_path as the user set it, so the gate
cannot have run after some defaulting of its own.

Regression tests/rvn_ple/test_rvn_nextn_draft_gate.py: on the 0047..0056
preimage 12 of its 13 cases fail - 11 because the predicate is absent, and the
one that drives _handle_eagle_family as "DID NOT RAISE" because the handler
walks past the missing gate. With this patch all 13 pass, and the module skips
cleanly (not a collection error) when RVN_PLE_TREE is unset, so a bare
``pytest tests/`` stays green on an unpatched tree. It pins the coupling the
gate depends on - _resolve_speculative_algorithm_alias still maps NEXTN to
EAGLE - and that the refusal leaves speculative_draft_model_path as the user
set it. Across the rest of tests/rvn_ple no case fails with this patch that
does not fail without it; the only cases it flips are two in patches
0058/0059's own suite, which call this predicate and so need it. Gate verdicts
against a real parse of
/models/rvn-qwen38-ple-nvfp4/config.json were also checked out of band: refusal
for NEXTN, None for STANDALONE, for an external draft path and for no
speculative decoding.

